' A PlantUML file of its own. The preview button in the editor's title bar
' opens a panel showing the diagram under the cursor; this file holds three,
' so the panel also lists them by id to pick from; its Copy button puts the
' one shown on the clipboard as a PNG, and Copy SVG as SVG text. Zoom to
' Area (Z) makes the next drag mark an area to zoom to, and Home, End and C
' scroll to the top, the bottom and the centre of the diagram. The Outline
' view lists the diagrams too, with what each declares, and each one folds
' from its start line. Above that line, Preview, Export SVG and Export PNG
' act on that diagram, and an error in any of them is listed in the Problems
' panel. Export All Diagrams in File as SVG writes one file per diagram,
' named by its id: images/checkout.svg and so on, beside this file. Export
' Diagram as PNG writes the one under the cursor.

@startuml(id=checkout)
actor Customer
participant "Web shop" as Shop
participant "Payment service" as Payments

Customer -> Shop : Place order
Shop -> Payments : Charge card
alt card accepted
  Payments --> Shop : Paid
  Shop --> Customer : Order confirmed
else card declined
  Payments --> Shop : Declined
  Shop --> Customer : Try another card
end
@enduml

@startuml(id=orders-model)
class Order {
  +id: string
  +placedAt: Date
  +total(): number
}
class LineItem {
  +quantity: number
}
class Product {
  +name: string
}
Order "1" *-- "*" LineItem
LineItem "*" --> "1" Product
@enduml

